[[File:Hijab_Niqab_Muslim_Veil.jpg|thumb|Hijab (left) and niqab (right) on display|Hijab (left) and niqab (right), two common forms of veiling]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|hejab}}<!--Collins-->, {{l|en|hijaab}}, {{l|en|hajib}}, {{l|en|hijabi}} {{qualifier|nonstandard}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|ar|حِجَاب||veil}}.
{{root|en|ar|ح ج ب}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/hɪˈd͡ʒɑːb/|/hɪˈd͡ʒæb/|ref2={{R:Dictionary.com}}}}<!--Dictionary.com actually verifies both pronunciations-->
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-hijab.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑːb|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|hi|jab}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|Islam}} The practice, among Muslim women, of covering the body after the [[age]] of [[puberty]] in front of non-related (non-family) [[adult]] [[males]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Jawairriya Abdallah-Shahid|title=Veiled Voices|isbn=1450053025|page=13
|passage=The belief that Muslim females observe '''hijab''' because men force them to do so insults some Muslim females who have based their decision on their understanding of Islam.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A traditional [[headscarf]] worn by Muslim women, covering the hair and neck.
#: {{cot|en|niqab|sheila|burka}}

